    "cli.surface.open.unknownResource": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Unknown surface '%@'. See: cmux surface ls --json"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "cli.surface.usage": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Usage: cmux surface ls [<machine>|local] [--refresh] [--json]\n       cmux surface open <resource> [--workspace <id|ref|index>] [--pane <id|ref>] [--left|--right|--up|--down|--tab] [--new] [--focus <true|false>]\n       cmux surface new-terminal --machine <id|local> [--cwd <dir>] [--name <name>] [--remote-workspace <ws_…>] [--workspace <id|ref|index>] [--no-open] [-- <command...>]\n       cmux surface new-display --machine <cloud-id> [--workspace <id|ref|index>] [--no-open] [--focus|--no-focus] [--json]\n       cmux surface resume set [flags] -- <argv...>\n       cmux surface resume set [flags] --shell <command>\n       cmux surface resume show [--json] [flags]\n       cmux surface resume get [--json] [flags]\n       cmux surface resume clear [flags]\n       cmux surface size|participants [--surface <id|ref|index>] [--json]\n       cmux surface size-policy <latest|smallest|largest|priority|fixed> [--cols <n> --rows <n>] [--surface <id|ref|index>]\n       cmux surface size-to-me|disconnect-others [--surface <id|ref|index>]\n       cmux surface size-counts <true|false|auto> [--participant <id>] [--surface <id|ref|index>]\n       cmux surface disconnect-participant <participant-id> [--surface <id|ref|index>]\n\nls / open / new-terminal / new-display: the surface catalog. Terminals, VNC screens and browsers\non This Mac and on every cloud machine are resources (`<machine>/<kind>/<key>`,\ne.g. local/terminal/<uuid>, vivid-newt/terminal/term_2f9c…, vivid-newt/display/display:1,\nvivid-newt/browser/port:3000); panes project them. `open` reuses the pane already\nshowing a resource unless --new; --pane with a side splits that pane on that side,\n--tab adds a tab to it. A local terminal moves to the destination (it is shown once).\n`new-terminal` creates a terminal on the machine (cloud: in its cmux-tui session).\n`new-display` creates a new VNC display on a cloud machine and opens it in the\nselected workspace unless `--no-open` is passed.\n`cmux vm tree` prints the same catalog.\n\nresume: attach restart command metadata to a terminal surface.\nPublic CLI bindings are stored for inspection and manual restore.\n\nFlags:\n  --workspace <id|ref|index>   Workspace context (default: $CMUX_WORKSPACE_ID)\n  --surface <id|ref|index>     Surface context (default: $CMUX_SURFACE_ID)\n  --window <id|ref|index>      Window context for workspace and surface refs/indexes\n  --cwd <path>             Working directory for restore (default: $PWD)\n  --name <name>            Display name for the binding\n  --kind <kind>            Binding kind, for example agent or tmux\n  --checkpoint <id>        Provider checkpoint or session id\n  --checkpoint-id <id>     Same as --checkpoint and takes precedence\n  --source <source>        Binding source label\n\nExamples:\n  cmux surface resume set --kind tmux --shell \"tmux attach -t work\"\n  cmux surface resume set --kind opencode --checkpoint ses_123 -- opencode --session ses_123\n  cmux surface resume show --json"
          }
        }
      }
    },
